From: Manish Verma <quic_maniverm@quicinc.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Apr 2023 15:57:43 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: align PPE RX fill ring size

Keep the EDMA RX fill ring independent from the WLAN PPE2TCL ring.  The
IPQ95xx QSDK profile uses 2048 fill descriptors with a 256-entry low
threshold even when PPE2TCL is enlarged to 8192 entries for high-rate
downlink traffic.

Using the PPE2TCL size for both rings retains 6144 unnecessary 2 KiB
buffers per radio without increasing the number of WLAN descriptors that
can be in flight.  Match the vendor profile while keeping the larger WLAN
ring and the existing refill budget.

Based-on: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-ppe/-/commit/30c5fe84ec4636f91eed86750c28903f64ff9433
Signed-off-by: Manish Verma <quic_maniverm@quicinc.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 
 #define ATH12K_PPE_DS_BUFFER_SIZE	2048
 #define ATH12K_PPE_DS_HEADROOM		130
+#define ATH12K_PPE_DS_RXFILL_SIZE	2048
 #define ATH12K_PPE_DS_RXFILL_THRESHOLD	256
 #define ATH12K_PPE_DS_RXFILL_BUDGET	128
 #define ATH12K_PPE_DS_TXCMPL_BUDGET	1024
@@ -649,7 +650,7 @@ int ath12k_ppe_ds_attach(struct ath12k_b
 	reg.reo2ppe_dma = ppe->reo2ppe_ring.paddr;
 	reg.ppe2tcl_count = DP_PPE2TCL_RING_SIZE;
 	reg.reo2ppe_count = DP_REO2PPE_RING_SIZE;
-	reg.rxfill_count = DP_PPE2TCL_RING_SIZE;
+	reg.rxfill_count = ATH12K_PPE_DS_RXFILL_SIZE;
 	reg.txcmpl_count = DP_REO2PPE_RING_SIZE;
 	reg.buffer_size = ATH12K_PPE_DS_BUFFER_SIZE;
 	reg.headroom = ATH12K_PPE_DS_HEADROOM;
